    {
      "data": {
        "text": "All requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_api_key.py** - fetches an API key from a managed secrets store (already provided).\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_db_secret.py** - fetches a database connection secret at runtime.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] parse_json_secret.py** - retrieves and parses a JSON-formatted secret.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] rotate_secret_version.py** - reads a specific secret version or staged value.\n5. **[HELPER] security_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Secret Management.\n6. **[HELPER] security_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Secret Management.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] rotation_summary.py** - Summarizes secret rotation status.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] secret_label_safety.py** - Checks secret labels and notes for unsafe text.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] secret_audit_embedding.py** - Embeds secret audit notes for semantic search.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] runbook_translate.py** - Translates secret-rotation runbook notes.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses Google Cloud Secret Manager as the concrete external provider, making it identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain utilities to support the secret management operations.",
